1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:01,800
Mark 6

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:07,700
He went away from there and came to his hometown, and his disciples followed him.

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:13,520
And on the Sabbath he began to teach in the synagogue, and many who heard him were astonished,

4
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,320
saying, Where did this man get these things?

5
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,600
What is the wisdom given to him?

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,400
How are such mighty works done by his hands?

7
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:26,880
Is not this the carpenter, the son of Mary, and brother of James, and Joses, and Judas,

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,440
and Simon?

9
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:30,160
And are not his sisters here with us?

10
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,380
And they took offense at him.

11
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:39,180
And Jesus said to them, A prophet is not without honor, except in his hometown, and among his

12
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:41,800
relatives, and in his own household.

13
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:48,200
And he could do no mighty work there, except that he laid his hands on a few sick people

14
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,740
and healed them, and he marveled because of their unbelief.

15
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:55,420
And he went about among the villages teaching.

16
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,420
And he called the church.

17
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:01,140
And he sent out twelve, and began to send them out two by two, and gave them authority

18
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:02,600
over the unclean spirits.

19
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:08,120
He charged them to take nothing for their journey except a staff, no bread, no bag,

20
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:12,520
no money in their belts, but to wear sandals and not put on two tunics.

21
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:18,880
And he said to them, Whenever you enter a house, stay there until you depart from there.

22
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:23,880
And if any place will not receive you, and they will not listen to you, when you leave,

23
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:26,400
shake off the dust that is on your feet.

24
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:28,380
As a testimony against them.

25
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:31,680
So they went out and proclaimed that people should repent.

26
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:36,580
And they cast out many demons, and anointed with oil many who were sick and healed them.

27
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,180
King Herod heard of it, for Jesus' name had become known.

28
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,540
Some said, John the Baptist has been raised from the dead.

29
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,660
That is why these miraculous powers are at work in him.

30
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:51,060
But others said, He is Elijah.

31
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:55,720
And others said, He is a prophet, like one of the prophets of old.

32
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,000
But when Herod heard of it, he said,

33
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:02,760
John, whom I beheaded, has been raised.

34
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:08,660
For it was Herod who had sent and seized John, and bound him in prison for the sake of Herodias,

35
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:11,660
his brother Philip's wife, because he had married her.

36
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,420
For John had been saying to Herod,

37
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:18,200
It is not lawful for you to have your brother's wife.

38
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:22,680
And Herodias had a grudge against him, and wanted to put him to death.

39
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,660
But she could not, for Herod feared John,

40
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:26,200
knowing that he would not be able to save him.

41
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:26,220
knowing that he would not be able to save him.

42
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:26,380
knowing that he would not be able to save him.

43
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,700
But he was a righteous and holy man, and he kept him safe.

44
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:34,920
When he heard him, he was greatly perplexed, and yet he heard him gladly.

45
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,660
But an opportunity came when Herod, on his birthday,

46
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:41,500
gave a banquet for his nobles and military commanders,

47
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:43,480
and the leading men of Galilee.

48
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,380
For when Herodias' daughter came in and danced,

49
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:49,460
she pleased Herod and his guests.

50
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,280
And the king said to the girl,

51
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:58,500
Ask me for whatever you wish, and I will give it to you.

52
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,080
And he vowed to her,

53
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:09,940
Whatever you ask me, I will give you, up to half of my kingdom.

54
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:13,180
And she went out and said to her mother,

55
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,360
For what should I ask?

56
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,020
And she said,

57
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:20,340
The head of John the Baptist.

58
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:24,940
And she came in immediately with haste to the king, and asked, saying,

59
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:31,320
I want you to give me at once the head of John the Baptist on a platter.

60
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:34,140
And the king was exceedingly sorry,

61
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:36,620
but because of his oaths and his guests,

62
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,680
he did not want to break his word to her.

63
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:43,760
And immediately the king sent an executioner with orders to bring John's head.

64
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:46,400
He went and beheaded him in the prison,

65
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:49,020
and brought his head on a platter and gave it to the girl.

66
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,260
And the girl,

67
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,240
gave it to her mother.

68
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,680
When his disciples heard of it,

69
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,500
they came and took his body and laid it in the tomb.

70
00:03:57,660 --> 00:04:01,800
The apostles returned to Jesus and told him all that they had done and taught.

71
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:03,200
And he said to them,

72
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:07,620
Come away by yourselves to a desolate place and rest a while.

73
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:09,880
For many were coming and going,

74
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:11,920
and they had no leisure even to eat.

75
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:15,280
And they went away in the boat to a desolate place by themselves.

76
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,580
Now many saw them going and recognized them,

77
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:20,180
and they ran there on foot,

78
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:22,260
from all the towns and got there ahead of them.

79
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:23,980
When he went ashore,

80
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,260
he saw a great crowd,

81
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,960
and he had compassion on them,

82
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,920
because they were like sheep without a shepherd.

83
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:32,180
And he began to teach them many things.

84
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:33,560
And when it grew late,

85
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,440
his disciples came to him and said,

86
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,700
This is a desolate place,

87
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:39,500
and the hour is now late.

88
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:43,940
Send them away to go into the surrounding countryside and villages,

89
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:46,140
and buy themselves something to eat.

90
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,020
But he answered them,

91
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,320
You give them something to eat,

92
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:52,340
and they said to him,

93
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,960
Shall we go and buy two hundred denarii worth of bread and give it to them to eat?

94
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,620
And he said to them,

95
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,680
How many loaves do you have?

96
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:02,700
Go and see.

97
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:05,380
And when they had found out, they said,

98
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,000
Five and two fish.

99
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:12,380
Then he commanded them all to sit down in groups on the green grass.

100
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:16,200
So they sat down in groups by hundreds and by fifties,

101
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:19,160
and taking the five loaves and the two fish,

102
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,320
he looked up to heaven,

103
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,480
and said a blessing,

104
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:22,800
and broke the loaves,

105
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,320
and gave them to the disciples to set before the people.

106
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,140
And he divided the two fish among them all,

107
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,240
and they all ate and were satisfied.

108
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:35,400
And they took up twelve baskets full of broken pieces and of the fish.

109
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:38,680
And those who ate the loaves were five thousand men.

110
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,360
Immediately he made his disciples get into the boat

111
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:44,520
and go before him to the other side,

112
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:45,500
to Bethsaida,

113
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,380
while he dismissed the crowd.

114
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,940
And after he had taken leave of them,

115
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:50,220
he went to the other side,

116
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:50,320
and he went to the other side,

117
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:50,340
and he went to the other side,

118
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:51,580
and he went up on the mountain to pray.

119
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:53,860
And when evening came,

120
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:55,220
the boat was out on the sea,

121
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,980
and he was alone on the land.

122
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:00,160
And he saw that they were making headway painfully,

123
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:01,960
for the wind was against them.

124
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,940
And about the fourth watch of the night,

125
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:06,020
he came to them,

126
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,140
walking on the sea.

127
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:09,180
He meant to pass by them,

128
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,420
but when they saw him walking on the sea,

129
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,520
they thought it was a ghost and cried out,

130
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,860
for they all saw him and were terrified.

131
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,320
But immediately he spoke to them and said,

132
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,920
Take heart!

133
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,240
It is I!

134
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,220
Do not be afraid!

135
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,780
And he got into the boat with them,

136
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:26,940
and the wind ceased.

137
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:29,280
And they were utterly astounded,

138
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,980
for they did not understand about the loaves,

139
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:33,540
but their hearts were hardened.

140
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,140
When they had crossed over,

141
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,780
they came to land at Gennesaret

142
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:39,180
and moored to the shore.

143
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,240
And when they got out of the boat,

144
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:43,220
the people immediately recognized him

145
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:45,140
and ran about the whole region

146
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:47,560
and began to bring the sick people on their beds

147
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,040
to wherever they heard he was.

148
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,440
And wherever he came,

149
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:53,660
in villages, cities, or countryside,

150
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,340
they laid the sick in the marketplaces

151
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,620
and implored him that they might touch

152
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:00,100
even the fringe of his garment.

153
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:02,900
And as many as touched it were made well.

